{"title":"Dreidimensionale Vektoren vervielfachen (2)","puid":"c-mat-11-algebra/x8teh2","path":"/../c-mat-11-algebra/topic-02-vektoren/block-05-vektoren-vervielfachen/level-04","type":"normal","voiceLang":"de","instruction":{"voice":"f5_2025","speaker":true,"autoplay":false},"textAlign":"left","hint":{"label":"Hilfe","text":{"text":"<m-yellow><t-yellow>&nbsp;Grundlagen&nbsp;</m-yellow></t-yellow>&nbsp;Wird ein Vektor <mat>rarrow(u)</mat> mit einer reellen Zahl <mat>r</mat> multipliziert, wird jede Koordinate des Vektors mit dieser Zahl multipliziert: <br><mat center='true'>r*vector(u_x,u_y,u_z)=vector(r*u_x,r*u_y,r*u_z)</mat><br>Die reelle Zahl <mat>r</mat> bezeichnet man als Skalar.<br><br><b>Beispiele:</b> <mat center='true'> 4*vector(1,2,4)=vector(4*1,4*2,4*4)= vector(4,8,16) </mat> <mat center='true'>   0.5*vector(9,-3,1)= vector(0.5 * 9, 0.5*(-3),0.5*1) = vector(4.5,-1.5,0.5)</mat>"}},"trainers":[{"trainer":"gap","calculator":true,"gapValidateMode":"literalSorted","gapMode":"write","instruction":{"text":"Multipliziere den Vektor mit dem Skalar.","speaker":true},"textAlign":"left","atoms":[{"b":"<mat>2*vector(1,2,3)=<gap>vector(2,4,6)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>3*vector(-2,0,4)=<gap>vector(-6,0,12)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>-1*vector(5,-3,2)=<gap>vector(-5,3,-2)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>0.5*vector(4,6,2)=<gap>vector(2,3,1)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>-2*vector(1.5,2,-1)=<gap>vector(-3,-4,2)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>1.5*vector(-2,3,-4)=<gap>vector(-3,4.5,-6)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>0.25*vector(8,-4,12)=<gap>vector(2,-1,3)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>-0.5*vector(6,2,-10)=<gap>vector(-3,-1,5)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>2.5*vector(0.4,-0.8,1.2)=<gap>vector(1,-2,3)</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<mat>-1.25*vector(-0.8,1.2,0.4)=<gap>vector(1,-1.5,-0.5)</gap></mat>"}]}],"parentTopic":{"title":"Vektoren","path":"/../c-mat-11-algebra/topic-02-vektoren/topic","puid":"c-mat-11-algebra/j8z5pp"},"parentBlock":{"title":"Vektoren vervielfachen","path":"/../c-mat-11-algebra/topic-02-vektoren/block-